Z||000010||Shaft||01-03-2001||05:39 PM||||I hate to see stories like that. A day or two after Christmas there was a car accident in Wooster, Ohio. Seven teenagers in a Buick were speeding down the road and lost control. The car hit a pole and I think it flipped a few times. 5 or 6 of the kids were killed in the accident. The driver was 16 (i think) and he had just gotten the car as a Christmas gift. After stories like this you'd think kids would learn to drive more responsibly.||||reg||1
Z||000011||FieroMaster88||01-03-2001||06:39 PM||||Well, I am 19 almost 20, and I sure as hell never drove like that.  I have lost 2 friends to automotive accidents, 1 was driving too fast and the other was not.  Another one of my friends just crashed his car, I cant beleive he walked away alive, he is another one who drives too fast!  I have 1 ticked, for an accident, I was not speeding, just didnt see the car stoped in front of me, oops.  <BR>Everyone can make a mistake, but when you are driving like that, you invlove other people.  I couldnt live with myslef if I knew my wreckless driving killed someone else.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig1_1.jpg"> <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster86<BR>88 Coupe 30,000 miles<BR>84 Indy Fiero (restoration Project)||||reg||1
