Z||000046||jerpro||01-06-2001||10:39 AM||||yet another fact not to allow teenagers to drive.<BR>In barcelona, Spain you can drink and smoke at 16 but you can't drive until you are 18.<BR>By the time you can drive you already know the effects of alcohol and can be more mature while driving/drinking.<BR>In spain you hear more about teenagers getting in accidents with scooters more than car drivers just because the car drivers are more mature.<BR>I think 18 should be the law for getting your lisense.<BR>I hope you guys can get him flowers or something. It is amazing to see how the fiero members around here care for others.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Only try your best, and if you don't succeed... TRY HARDER.||||reg||1
Z||000047||KnightRyder31||01-06-2001||11:03 AM||||I feel great sorro for this guy in the Fiero.<BR>And I also feel sorry for that poor fiero!<BR>It would be great if this guy joined the forum after he recovered.<BR>Also, I must agree with Fiero Lisa; age doesn't always mean everything. I think there can be a 40 year old driver who is a wreckless and inconsiderate driver. I am not saying that this 16 year old kid was not a bad driver(because he really is) but not all young driver's are bad. I started driving when I was 15 years old and nine months. And I have never been in a acendent. I may have been pulled over for speeding, but if and when I speed, I do it in a smart manner. I am now 18, and I know that I am a very good driver. I think this kid should get prison time...give him time to think about what he has done. Ending someone's life has got to be the worst feeling that you can feel, it's going to stay with this 16 year old boy for the rest of his life, jail or not.<P>||||reg||1
