Z||000049||KRMFiero||01-06-2001||09:53 PM||||Wow, more i look at that, most of my friends tell me that  If you hit anything in a Fiero, your dead... even though that car is totaled, they guy lived.... but look at what hit him a truck 3 times the size of it,   I think most other people would have died with different cars if they hit that (well the subaru guy did i think)<P>||||reg||1
Z||000050||fiero56||01-06-2001||10:10 PM||||The Subaru hit the Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000051||chahn72||01-06-2001||11:01 PM||||The man in the Fiero is Anthony Barber.  He received your flowers today, and let me say that we are so overwhelmed by your support.  Words cannot express what your gift has done for us and his family.<P>I'm not sure how much you all have read, but let me let you know who I am and my connection to Anthony.<P>My name is Chip, and my sister Abby is Anthony's girlfriend.  She was driving the Toyota Turcel that was in front of Anthony.  The Turcel is also totaled, though not nearly as badly as the Fiero.  Abby was released from the hospital the same day as the accident.  She's a little sore, and they're still keeping tabs on her to make sure, but her injuries are the type that only time will heal.<P>Anthony suffered a broken femur and two contusions on his brain.  He had surgery on his leg yesterday(they fixed his nose the at the same time).  Surgery went very well.  The surgeon indicated that the break was very clean, and he could probably put weight on it almost immediately.  He is out of intensive care, and has been upgraded to serious/stable condition, and is now in progressive care.  He is sometimes awake, and aware.  He recognizes people and is talking (sometimes not making sense).  <P>Tonight I am told he was actually sitting up and feeding himself.  <P>The road to recovery will be a long one, but easier because of the support we have seen from people such as yourselves.<P>If there is an administrator of this forum, please send me an email address if you're interested in ongoing updates.<P>Once again, both of our families thank you for your kindness in this horrible time.||||reg||1
Z||000052||Cooter||01-06-2001||11:32 PM||||Right now Anthony has almost 2000 friends pulling for him. Our thoughts and prayers are with your family, friend and the other victoms of this terrible crime. If there is anything this forum's members can do to help, please ask.||||reg||1
Z||000053||mrfiero||01-07-2001||12:13 AM||||Thanks for the update Chip.  I'm/we're glad to see his condition is improving and that your sister/Anthony's girlfriend fared well in the crash.<P>You can e-mail me updates if you wish and I can then re-post them here.  My e-mail address is  mrfiero@juno.com<P><BR>||||reg||14
Z||000054||Notchit||01-07-2001||01:37 AM||||I cannot believe how awesome this boardroom is! i mean, you all cared soo much for a fellow Fiero owner and showed overwhelming kindness. It puts my faith back into humanity...<P>------------------<BR>Seein Red<BR>'85 Fiero GT<BR>ICQ#: 56708070<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Outside_side2(sml2).jpg"> <BR>_________________________||||reg||14
Z||000055||Cheever2||01-07-2001||01:42 AM||||Thank you very much Chip for letting us know what's going on.  Speedy recovery to all.  Please return, or like mrfiero said, email him.  We'd also certainly like to hear from Anthony on here someday.<BR>||||reg||6
